---
title: "skyBlip Go and Bravo guides and first steps"
nav_title: Guides
description: "Install your Go or Bravo, then find the controls, read the lights and set up your device for your first flight."
share_image: radar
updated_on: "2026-11-20"
---

<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>Find the right guide for your Go or Bravo</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">Just got your device? <%= link_to_page "install", label: "Start by installing it" %>. If Briefing says the device is ready, open its guide.</p>
</header>

<section id="install" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Install</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "self-test.png", alt: "The self-test page, with each component's name and test result, including TEMP NRF52840 marked NOT FOUND" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "install", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>Put skyBlip on your Go or Bravo from your browser. At every start, the Go checks its radio, GPS and barometer, and does not run without them.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= content_image_tag "pages/mount/go-plus-clamp.avif", alt: "skyBlip Go+ on a white LilyGO T-Echo Plus beside the crab clamp with an orange handle that holds it on the glareshield", class: "guide-photo" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "mount", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>Click a Go or a Go+ onto a ball joint clamped to the glareshield, with the parts we tested, place its antenna, and hang Bravo by its lanyard.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Start with your device</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= content_image_tag "pages/index/skyblip-go-techo.avif", alt: "skyBlip Go with its antenna and traffic radar on the e-paper screen", class: "guide-photo" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "go-first-steps", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>Switch on Go, read its radar and set your aircraft type or callsign.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= content_image_tag "pages/skyblip-bravo/seeed-x1.avif", alt: "skyBlip Bravo on a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, a black case with one round button", class: "guide-photo photo-x1" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "bravo-first-steps", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>Find the button and light. See traffic in your navigation app or on the paired Go.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="signature">With a Tango, open both guides. Go shows the traffic and Bravo adds to what it receives.</p>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">In flight</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "far-all.png", alt: "The radar page in PLOT ALL, traffic inside the ring and on the band around it" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radar" %></h3>
      <p>The radar keeps your direction of travel at the top and shows each aircraft's predicted path for the next minute. An alarm tells you where to look, and a list shows nearby aircraft.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "sixpack.png", alt: "The six-dial page" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "instruments" %></h3>
      <p>Six dials show GPS and barometer readings, for fun. The battery level sits above the middle dial. On the Go+, a g-meter records the flight's peak loads.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "astern-all.png", alt: "The radar page in PLOT ALL with a group of aircraft behind you" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "displays" %></h3>
      <p>See every page, every menu and every on-screen request, with the radar in both display modes.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-radar.png", alt: "The settings menu" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "controls" %></h3>
      <p>Two controls, a pad and a button, let you change settings in the radar menu, enter your callsign on the device, and open diagnostic pages.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "off-flat-battery.png", alt: "The screen of a device that has switched off because its battery is empty" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "power" %></h3>
      <p>See what it waits for on the apron, what it looks like when off, and how the battery warns as it drains.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= screen_image_tag "confirm.png", alt: "The authorisation prompt on the screen" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "phone", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>See traffic in your navigation app. Use Briefing to change settings or update skyBlip.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">How it works</h2>
  <div class="guide-cards">
    <article>
      <%= render "shared/second", compact: true %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radio" %></h3>
      <p>One radio uses four time slots a second and receives signals from two systems in the same slot.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= render "shared/cycle", compact: true %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "timing" %></h3>
      <p>The serial picks the seconds of a 20&nbsp;s cycle, the parity of the second picks the channel, and a draw redone every second picks the millisecond.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= render "shared/flight_state", compact: true %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "gps" %></h3>
      <p>A fix that must settle and land before 450&nbsp;ms, the pulse that starts each second, and flight decided from ground speed alone.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <%= render "shared/advisory_ring", compact: true %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "traffic" %></h3>
      <p>One advisory ring of 3&nbsp;km and 300&nbsp;m, no advisories on the ground, six missed reports to drop a target, and formation flying.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">For the curious</h2>
  <div class="resource-cards">
    <article>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "see-and-avoid" %></h3>
      <p>The published figures for see and avoid cover field of view, the sector scanned, an aircraft's apparent size and reaction time.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "roadmap", label_type: :nav %></h3>
      <p>Read about skyBlip Panel for cockpit displays and skyPost stations for relaying traffic around an airfield.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
